    "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11132": {
      "title": "Ranked Faculty and Program Director",
      "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Ranked Faculty and Program Director - Radiation Therapy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Ranked Faculty and Program Director - Radiation Therapy Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Ranked Faculty and Program Director - Radiation Therapy Division Academic Affairs Department/Office Radiation Therapy Position Summary Information Advertisement The Radiation Therapy Program at St. Catherine University in St. Paul, Minnesota, invites applications for a full-time (1.0 FTE ) ranked faculty position on a 9-over 12- month professional practice contract. This faculty member will also hold the role of Program Director for Radiation Therapy. Individuals interested in remote employment may pursue this role if they live in any of the following states: AR, CA, CO, DE, FL, IL, IN, MD, MA, MI, MS, NC, NY, OR, PA, TN, TX, UT, VT, VA, DC, WI. This faculty member will teach the equivalent of six courses (24 credits) a year. The The Radiation Therapy program is a bachelor’s degree program within the College for Adults (CfA). St. Kate’s can enroll up to 14 students in each year-long cohort. The program is offered entirely online, and there is one other full-time faculty member who also serves as the clinical coordinator. Search Process The position will remain open until filled with a priority deadline of Monday, September 21, 2026. Selected candidates will participate in an online interview with the search committee, and two to four individuals will then be selected for a longer virtual interview. This will include meetings with various university partners, a teaching and vision presentation, and interviews with the committee and dean. The goal is for the new program director to begin on November 30, 2026. Program Director Role Program directors have several additional responsibilities beyond teaching: Curriculum Management and Accreditation Lead, compile, and submit accreditation materials to the Joint Review Committee on Education in Radiologic Technology ( JRCERT ), including annual reports and program changes Lead assessment of student learning and programmatic effectiveness process Faculty Staffing and Oversight Recruit, evaluate, and recommend faculty for hire to ensure adequate program and course staffing Support faculty in university evaluation processes for contract renewal and promotion Academic Program Administration Create and manage the schedule of courses Lead the student application process Learn and utilize various internal university tools and systems to ensure effective program delivery Additional information can be found in the accreditation standards: the JRCERT outlines expected responsibilities in Standard 3.3 . Working Environment and Expectations The selected candidate can work completely remote, from any of the states listed above. Currently, the program offers live virtual sessions for students on Wednesdays between 9:00 am and 3:00 pm ( CST ). However, faculty, with university support, are moving to an asynchronous learning format with an implementation goal of fall 2028. Additionally, the program director will need to attend approximately 3 to 5 hours of meetings each week, scheduled between 8:00 am and 4:30 pm ( CST ), plus another 2 hours of meetings per week that they schedule and lead during these times. Most work will be deadline-driven and require self-direction and prioritization. This will include grading, course preparation, university service, and program director responsibilities. As a Professional Practice faculty member, individuals can pursue, with the Dean’s approval, practice within the field of Radiation Therapy. Program Information The Program Director will work closely with the program’s other faculty member who also holds the Clinical Coordinator role. Students in the program currently complete their required clinical experiences at hospitals and clinics within the Twin Cities. Across the institution, there is an effort to explore growth opportunities. Applicants who can embrace this mindset and help to identify opportunities to leverage the online nature of this program and bring the degree to students outside of the Twin Cities are encouraged to apply. Program growth will likely require additional adjunct or potential full-time faculty. The Radiation Therapy program at St. Kate’s has a long-standing tradition of excellence. Students progress through the program, pass their certification exam on their first attempt, and secure jobs at rates routinely above 90%. The program is accredited through the JRCERT , and its next scheduled accreditation review is in 2029. The program is part of the Henrietta Schmoll School of Health Sciences ( HSSHS ). With 18 degree programs and approximately 100 faculty, the HSSHS is the largest of St. Kate’s three schools. Degrees are offered to students at all levels, from the associate to the doctoral level. A key distinguishing factor is the school’s programs’ shared focus on ecological approaches to health, intercultural competency, and interprofessional collaboration. Faculty and staff will find ample opportunities for support for teaching, professional practice, and scholarly activities. The Institute of Simulation and Interprofessional Learning (I- SAIL ) provides resources and expertise to support developing and implementing high-impact educational activities within HSSHS and the School of Nursing. The St. Kate’s Teaching Hub offers resources and a platform for teaching and scholarly activities that foster pedagogical innovation and student success. The Hub supports faculty and staff by providing professional development opportunities and a forum for learning and exchange on issues at the forefront of higher education. Additionally, St. Kate’s has a growing academic technology team that offers training and support to faculty members who teach online. Minimum Qualifications Proficient in curriculum design, evaluation, instruction, program administration, and academic advising; 3 years of clinical experience in the professional discipline; 2 years of experience as an instructor in a JRCERT -accredited program; Holds current American Registry of Radiologic Technologists certification and registration, or equivalent, in radiation therapy. Master’s degree Individuals who do not have a master’s degree may apply but must complete a master’s degree within the first 3 years of employment. The institution will provide tuition remission for St. Kate’s graduate programs , including the online MBA Program. Preferred Qualifications Previous Clinical Coordinator or Program Director experience Experience teaching online Clinical or professional organization leadership experience EEO Statement Compensation: Annual wage is $67,281 – $85,312 depending on qualifications and experience. The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. Benefits: Employees at St. Kate’s feel a deep connection to the University’s Mission and Vision, and they live their values at work. Benefits available to full-time employees include: Fourteen (14) paid holidays and paid “gift” days when the University is closed. Free tuition for employees and reduced tuition for their families after one year of service Health, dental, and vision insurance 403b retirement plan access Accrued sick time Specific information on all of our available benefits for full-time employees can be found HERE . St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to “love of neighbor without distinction” and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups that have traditionally had less representation in higher education are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for FACULTY Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding and diverse faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220376-FAC Posting Start Date 09/04/2026 Application Deadline 10/15/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11142": {
      "title": "St. Catherine Employment Site",
      "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Campus Life Operations Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Campus Life Operations Manager Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Campus Life Operations Manager Division Student Affairs, Equity and Belonging Department/Office Student Cntr/Activities Position Summary Information Advertisement The Student Affairs, Equity, and Belonging Department at St. Catherine University invites applications for a full-time Campus Life Operations Manager position. The Campus Life Operations Manager is serves as a key member of the Campus Life Team and is responsible for the oversight of the university Information and Campus Life desks, including recruiting, training, scheduling and supervision of student workers. The Operations Manager also manages day-to-day operations of these critical university services, ranging from supporting students to directing community members to campus. The Operations Manager contributes student communications including updating websites, preparing newsletters, and event logistics. Duties will include: Manage the student employment program for the Information Center and Campus Life Desk, supervising approximately 35–50 student employees and 2–4 Lead Student Workers. Coordinate the full student employment cycle each semester for desk workers, including recruitment, interviewing, hiring, onboarding, training, scheduling, performance management, evaluation, recognition, and offboarding. Develop and maintain staffing plans that provide appropriate coverage for two customer service desks, while responsibly managing student employment resources. Develop student employee position descriptions, expectations, training materials, operating procedures, evaluation tools, meeting cadence, and accountability systems. Clearly define the Lead Student Worker role as a student leadership position with responsibility for supporting peers and daily desk operations, defining roles each semester to meet operational needs while creating a meaningful experience with increasing responsibilities. Promote inclusive, accessible, professional, and student-centered customer service practices. Manage the daily operations of the Information Center, Campus Life Desk, and Student Organization Center in collaboration with Campus Life leadership. Ensure both service desks are appropriately staffed, organized, supplied, and prepared to provide consistent service to students, employees, and visitors. Develop, document, maintain, and regularly review operating procedures for services provided through the desks. Oversee operational processes including: Metro Transit pass distribution and tracking Locker rentals and annual locker cleanout Lost and found Equipment and resource checkout General campus information and referrals Student organization resources and checkouts Campus Life forms, materials, and student resources Maintain accurate logs, records, inventory systems, and operational documentation, monitoring volume, usage and type of service to inform staffing, desk hours, resource allocation, and operational improvements. Coordinate office supplies, equipment, materials, purchasing, and inventory for Campus Life operations. Troubleshoot day-to-day operational issues and determine when concerns should be elevated to Campus Life leadership. Provide administrative support to functions related to Orientation and Honors and Awards programming. Update and maintain Campus Life and Residence Life websites, online resources, forms, shared files, and other administrative systems. Oversee the creation of the weekly student engagement newsletter Participate in departmental meetings, planning, assessment, and continuous improvement efforts and committee meetings as appropriate. Assist with large Student Affairs and campus events with day/night-of logistics support. Maintain effective relationships with campus and community partners. Foster positive and professional relationships with students. Perform other duties consistent with the operational and administrative responsibilities of the position Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Minimum of 2 years of experience in supervising employees Experience scheduling to cover business operations Exceptional organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Commitment to equity, diversity, and inclusion in higher education. Proficiency with Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, and/or student engagement platforms Preferred Qualifications Experience working in higher education Experience in website design Experience training employees EEO Statement Compensation: Annual wage is $41,154 – $51,770 depending on qualifications and experience. The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. Benefits: Employees at St. Kate’s feel a deep connection to the University’s Mission and Vision, and they live their values at work. Benefits available to full-time employees include: Fourteen (14) paid holidays and paid “gift” days when the University is closed. Free tuition for employees and reduced tuition for their families after one year of service Health, dental, and vision insurance 403b retirement plan access Accrued sick time Specific information on all of our available benefits for full-time employees can be found HERE . St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to “love of neighbor without distinction” and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of all religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for STAFF Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220858-STAFF Posting Start Date 09/08/2026 Application Deadline 09/28/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter References Optional Documents 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11149": {
      "title": "St. Catherine Employment Site",
      "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | TRIO Success Coach Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan TRIO Success Coach Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title TRIO Success Coach Division Academic Affairs Department/Office SPREE - Grants Position Summary Information Advertisement The SPREE – Grants Program at St. Catherine University invites applications for a full-time TRIO Success Coach position. The TRIO Success Coach will fulfill the role as described in the TRIO SSS grant, serving as the primary academic advisor for assigned TRIO SSS students, developing and implementing programming for TRIO SSS students, and supporting program operations including outreach, recordkeeping, and evaluation. The Success Coach will employ a holistic approach, including financial aid support; resource referrals; graduate education preparation; support accessing community-engaged learning, career development, global studies, and other high-impact opportunities; and consideration of how other aspects of students’ lives affect academics. The TRIO Success Coach will: Manage and advise caseload of 60-70 TRIO SSS participants. Deliver proactive advising services to participants. Refer to appropriate campus offices based on assessed need. Communicate with participants’ faculty and academic support staff to surface and remediate any challenges or concerns. Design individual student success plans. Document and track student progress against agreed upon goals and program expectations outlined in success plans. Plan, coordinate, and deliver enrichment events that support student success. Coordinate with Student Accessibility and Accommodations, Career Development, Office for Scholarly Engagement, Financial Literacy, Centers for Equity and Belonging, and other offices/programs to provide co-curricular activities and opportunities for participants. Support major processes required to accomplish grant goals. Assist with recruitment and eligibility screening for program participants. Present information about the TRIO SSS program to relevant audiences on and off campus. Regularly update participant files to maintain complete and accurate program records. Assist director with data collection to support program reporting requirements. Participate in regular Academic Advising, TRIO SSS , and other relevant meetings. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Education, Psychology, Counseling, Student Affairs, or a related field. Undergraduate academic advising or related experience. Experience supporting student populations similar to TRIO SSS -eligible students (low-income, first-generation, and students with disabilities). Strong analytical and communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office and Google Workplace. Ability to manage multiple time-sensitive projects while maintaining high-contact relationships with students. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree. Experience advising students in TRIO programs. Experience applying academic advising approaches and retention best practices in higher education. Three or more years of experience within a college or university advising, career, tutoring, or related department. Demonstrated ability to deliver workshops and training. We seek creative, adaptable staff who enjoy working in a university climate that promotes cultural diversity, multicultural understanding, and cultural fluency. Consistent with the university’s commitment to women, diversity, and social justice, preference will be given to candidates who manifest these themes in their experience and service. EEO Statement Compensation: Annual wage is $42,474 – $49,500 depending on qualifications and experience. The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. Benefits: Employees at St. Kate’s feel a deep connection to the University’s Mission and Vision, and they live their values at work. Benefits available to full-time employees include: Fourteen (14) paid holidays and paid “gift” days when the University is closed. Free tuition for employees and reduced tuition for their families after one year of service Health, dental, and vision insurance 403b retirement plan access Accrued sick time Specific information on all of our available benefits for full-time employees can be found HERE . St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to “love of neighbor without distinction” and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of all religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for STAFF Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220838-STAFF Posting Start Date 09/14/2026 Application Deadline 10/04/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document 1 Transcripts Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 References 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
