    "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11131": {
      "title": "Director of Campus Life",
      "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Director of Campus Life Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Director of Campus Life Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Director of Campus Life Division Student Affairs, Equity and Belonging Department/Office Student Cntr/Activities Position Summary Information Advertisement The Student Center/Activities Department at St. Catherine University invites applications for a full-time Director of Campus Life position. The Director of Campus Life provides strategic day-to-day leadership to the department of Campus Life supervising professional and student staff to ensure delivery of student-ready, safe, inclusive, equitable and responsive student services. The Director will lead the overall design, planning, direction and administration of the operational, programmatic, financial and staffing functions of the Campus Life working collaboratively with a diverse team to deliver engaging new student orientation programs, provide inclusive and creative student activities, support student clubs and organizations, and provide services to the community through the Information Desk. The Director of Campus Life serves as as a key member of the Student Affairs, Equity and Belonging Leadership Team The Director of Campus life will: Hire, train, and provide feedback and performance evaluations to Campus Life supervisees. Oversee the day-to day operations of Campus Life, including the Student Organization Center, the University Information Desk, and student clubs and organizations, to include staff development and supervision, oversight of facilities, budgeting development and management, marketing, communications and assessment of services and student learning outcomes. In collaboration with the Director of Residence Life, provide guidance to Residence Life team members with cross-assignments to Campus Life initiatives .Oversee and manage all registered student organizations including financial, risk, programmatic, operational, programming, assessment, and administrative management. Advise/Co-Advise student government organizations for all three colleges Oversee with support of the Associate Director, student leadership development and training programs including, but not limited to SGA , campus activity board ( SEEK ) leaders, orientation leaders and student organization officers. Ensure programs assist students, student organizations, student leaders, and advisors in gaining the knowledge, skills, and abilities necessary to perform leadership functions such as event planning, budget development, policy interpretation, conflict management, basic governance and leadership skills. With the support of a cross-campus committee and the Associate and Assistant Directors, design, plan, and implement engaging, inclusive, and accessible new student Orientation programs Leverage cross-campus working groups, Campus Life staff and student organizations to lead the development and coordination of cultural, social, and recreational activities that reflect the University’s mission and diverse population and foster campus traditions and milestones. With Student Affairs, Equity and Belonging divisional leadership, develop leadership training and micro-credentialing opportunities for students. Serve as a student conduct hearing officer. Serve on-call in university duty rotation, responding to emergencies after hours and on weekends when on call. Develop and maintain appropriate protocols and procedure manuals for the department, Division, and University as necessary. Represent Campus Life on designated committees, working collaboratively to engage partners in programs and initiatives and co-leading campus working groups. Communicate regularly with Student Affairs, Equity and Belonging leadership and campus stakeholders. Assist with large Student Affairs and campus events with day/night-of logistics support. Demonstrate timely responses to student concerns including follow up with students who have been referred to the Director due to complicated or unresolved issues within area of responsibility Maintain effective relationships with campus and community partners. Foster positive and professional relationships with students. Perform other duties consistent with the operational and administrative responsibilities of the position. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a related field (communication, education, social work, education, psychology, etc.) Five (5) years of full-time experience leading higher education (or higher education adjacent) initiatives related to student development, student engagement, residential living, and leadership development. Demonstrated experience of supervising full-time professional staff Demonstrated positive impacts across diverse populations with culturally relevant program development and administration Experience in decision-making, budget management, and ability to work effectively in a team relationship. Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing with proficiency in analytical and critical thinking with the ability to make decisions following appropriate consultation. Higher education experience related to working within student affairs units such as residence life, student activities, orientation, and campus events. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in a related field (communication, higher education administration, counseling, social work, education, psychology, etc.) 2+ years supervising full-time professional staff Experience in new student orientation Experience advising student government associations Experience related to managing several divergent tasks simultaneously, managing change, and advising student organizations. Experience with on-call/emergency response Experience with student conduct EEO Statement Compensation: Annual wage is $56,781 – $82,200 depending on qualifications and experience. The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. Benefits: Employees at St. Kate’s feel a deep connection to the University’s Mission and Vision, and they live their values at work. Benefits available to full-time employees include: Fourteen (14) paid holidays and paid “gift” days when the University is closed. Free tuition for employees and reduced tuition for their families after one year of service Health, dental, and vision insurance 403b retirement plan access Accrued sick time Specific information on all of our available benefits for full-time employees can be found HERE . St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to “love of neighbor without distinction” and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of all religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for STAFF Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220857-STAFF Posting Start Date 09/09/2026 Application Deadline 09/21/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter References Optional Documents 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
