    "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11151": {
      "title": "St. Catherine Employment Site",
      "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Ranked Principal MPAS Faculty- Full Time Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Ranked Principal MPAS Faculty- Full Time Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Ranked Principal MPAS Faculty- Full Time Division Academic Affairs Department/Office Physician Assistant Program Position Summary Information Advertisement The Master of Physician’s Assistant Program at St. Catherine University invites applications for a 12-month full-time Ranked Principal MPAS Faculty position. The MPAS Program seeks a collaborative, innovative, and student-centered educator who will contribute to the delivery of high-quality physician assistant education including program assessment, evaluation, and continuous quality improvement. The successful candidate will work closely with the Program Director, Medical Director, Curriculum Director, and faculty team to support student success, curricular excellence, and ongoing assessment and accreditation compliance. Primary Responsibilities This position encompasses three major areas of responsibility: 1. Didactic Teaching – 60% The faculty member will provide instruction in areas of expertise and program need, with a primary emphasis on clinical medicine, history-taking and physical examination skills, and primary care practice. Responsibilities include: Teaching in classroom, laboratory, simulation, and small-group settings Facilitating active learning and case-based educational experiences Assessing student performance and providing timely feedback Assisting with curriculum development, implementation, and revision Supporting student scholarly, quality improvement, and capstone projects as assigned 2. Assessment and Evaluation – 20% The faculty member will participate in the implementation, management, and continuous improvement of the program’s comprehensive assessment and evaluation system. Responsibilities include: Participating in programmatic assessment activities to measure student learning outcomes, curricular effectiveness, and program performance Collecting, analyzing, interpreting, and reporting assessment and evaluation data Monitoring student progression, academic performance, and remediation outcomes Supporting continuous quality improvement initiatives through data-informed decision making Collaborating with faculty and the Program Director to develop and implement assessment strategies aligned with program outcomes Preparing reports, dashboards, and documentation to support accreditation activities and institutional reporting requirements Ensuring assessment and evaluation processes remain aligned with ARC -PA Standards and University expectations Supporting accreditation readiness and ongoing compliance efforts 3. Student support and development – 15% Participating in student advising, mentoring, remediation, and academic support Supporting student scholarly, quality improvement, and capstone projects as assigned Facilitating student professional development, including career advising, leadership development, and preparation for clinical practice and certification examinations. Promoting student engagement, well-being, and inclusivity through collaboration with faculty, staff, and university support services. Additional Faculty Responsibilities – 5% Faculty members are expected to actively contribute to the academic mission of the MPAS Program and St. Catherine University through: Participation in student admissions, recruitment, and selection activities Serve in program, school, and university committees, including faculty governance Engagement in scholarly activity and professional development Participation in faculty meetings, retreats, and strategic planning initiatives Collaboration with clinical partners and interprofessional colleagues Maintenance of professional certification, licensure, and clinical expertise The selected individual will demonstrate a commitment to collaborative education, innovation in teaching and assessment, and to preparing compassionate, competent physician assistants dedicated to serving diverse communities. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must possess a master’s degree or doctoral degree in a health-related discipline. Physician Assistant Candidates Current NCCPA certification Current Minnesota PA license or eligibility for licensure in Minnesota Minimum of two years of clinical practice experience Physician, Nurse Practitioner, or Other Allied Health Candidates Current professional certification and/or licensure in discipline Minnesota licensure or eligibility for licensure Minimum of two years of professional clinical experience Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience in higher education, health professions education, or clinical training programs Experience with assessment, program evaluation, outcomes measurement, or accreditation processes Familiarity with ARC -PA standards and accreditation requirements Experience in curriculum development and instructional design Experience mentoring students in academic or clinical environments, including research, scholarly, quality improvement, or capstone projects Demonstrated scholarly activity, including presentations, publications, or research EEO Statement Compensation: Annual wage is dependent on qualifications and experience: Assistant Professor: $87,000 – $95,000 Associate Professor: $105,000 – $115,000 The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. Benefits: Employees at St. Kate’s feel a deep connection to the University’s Mission and Vision, and they live their values at work. Benefits available to full-time employees include: Fourteen (14) paid holidays and paid “gift” days when the University is closed. Free tuition for employees and reduced tuition for their families after one year of service Health, dental, and vision insurance 403b retirement plan access Accrued sick time Specific information on all of our available benefits for full-time employees can be found HERE . St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to “love of neighbor without distinction” and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups that have traditionally had less representation in higher education are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for FACULTY Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding and diverse faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220367-FAC Posting Start Date 09/14/2026 Application Deadline 10/10/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume or Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Interests Optional Documents Resume Curriculum Vitae Letter of Recommendation 1 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
